# NOVA Reader — environment variables
#
# Core reading, saving, offline storage, and on-device WebAssembly/WebGPU summarization
# require NO environment variables or external API keys.
#
# Optional server-side environment variables:

# GEMINI_API_KEY: Optional server-side key used by POST /api/translate for high-fidelity
# article and localized summary translation. When omitted, NOVA Reader automatically
# falls back to a server-side translation relay so translation still works out of the box.
GEMINI_API_KEY="MY_GEMINI_API_KEY"

# APP_URL: Optional URL where the app is hosted (injected automatically in Cloud Run / AI Studio).
APP_URL="MY_APP_URL"

# Set automatically by Next.js / CI (do not put these in .env files):
#   NODE_ENV=production   `npm run build` / `npm start` (enables the service worker
#                         and the strict Content-Security-Policy without 'unsafe-eval')
#   CI=true               set by GitHub Actions; makes the e2e tests stricter
#
# Never commit real secrets. `.env*` files are ignored by git except this one.
